34ef4660a4b62ead5bf1f91dfb438725115d7289eb41fe950d2ed803d" :answer-field/choices ["q-340528/field-2/45748e934ef4660a4b62ead5bf1f91dfb438725115d7289eb41fe950d2ed803d" "q-340528/field-2/61bbf40bf0728127bc167767b5af83361c3acbddac67f4a51d278c010c10af58"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340528" :question/id #uuid "0a425ff5-8d1c-54df-a9b1-2af91c0d28d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-340528" :question/problem "$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nGiven the inner product on the set of continuous functions over $x\\in [0,2\\pi ]$ defined above, select the correct options below.$\\,$\n$⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),1⟩=$ \n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\,$\nThe functions $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)$ and $g(x)=1$ \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Evaluating the inner product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),1⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(0-0) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)$ and $g(x)=1$ \n$\\text{are orthogonal}$ with respect to the inner product." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-340528/field-1" "q-340528/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fadf4f64-3569-56b2-98e1-f6681892054a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-340528"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-340669/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "6d71a200-4fde-56e3-89eb-612366eaa5da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340669/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "fa0b26cf-59c1-5be7-8143-094a25436d90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/