340669/field-2/45748e934ef4660a4b62ead5bf1f91dfb438725115d7289eb41fe950d2ed803d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340669" :question/id #uuid "3d6ca311-b229-51f5-b6ee-b805697465fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-340669" :question/problem "$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nGiven the inner product on the set of continuous functions over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ defined above, select the correct options below.$\\,$\n$⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x),1⟩=$ \n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\,$\nThe functions $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)$ and $g(x)=1$ \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Evaluating the inner product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x),1⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)]}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{6}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-6\\pi )) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{6}(1-1) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)$ and $g(x)=1$ $\\text{are orthogonal}$ with respect to the inner product." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-340669/field-1" "q-340669/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fadf4f64-3569-56b2-98e1-f6681892054a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-340669"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-340677/field-1/986e06f062dcc0ad37fbb185f7e0d56b0fd8e74b571035e7dc0af3d06af89951" :answer/id #uuid "4185591d-cf23-56fb-97ac-67cc6af5b0c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340677/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "a978ddc4-0dc7-5677-b7aa-e220660ce360" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340677/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "3cc09566-4118-5f8c-bcf