adbaa9-3704-55c5-b06c-10ecac00be61" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }({x}^{3}+5x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340638/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "a4bb4dd8-e21b-5d8d-b4e2-fdfd452cd4c1" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-340638/field-3/aa772e7d2fc132d53d15e08aff5961c21387632f0d92ccd2d06c06096ca257e5" :answer-field/choices ["q-340638/field-3/caceb1c6c66806fc7ac9f8ceeac483b584fb9207d7e9a350984c325f7bcc7017" "q-340638/field-3/1f45e19b3325533845bb26e03f5e7ef2c9d153a720b5dd70782910f600225133" "q-340638/field-3/cce9f716b8f939b202dfd1e5f98504e9c482c918eef9640f7cefb463a0744fc2" "q-340638/field-3/c21966a44f0256a1e84c6c88a8e6094e28390cb621205d9c41b88b14f07ebdac" "q-340638/field-3/aa772e7d2fc132d53d15e08aff5961c21387632f0d92ccd2d06c06096ca257e5" "q-340638/field-3/a4c88eac0996a22fbcaedae9c883bde66327083f967753c1b919258a6d391cc3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340638" :question/id #uuid "df849e8a-df1b-5b2f-bbc1-5b6e2ad9aeb2" :question/math-academy-id "q-340638" :question/problem "Let $F(x)={x}^{3}+5x$ for $x\\in R,$ and let $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of $F$ from $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ to $x\\in R.$ The Fourier series of $f$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the expression for the coefficient ${a}_{6}$ below, where $⟨\\,,⟩$ denotes the usual inner product on functions over $[-\\pi ,\\pi ).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{6} & ={{field-1}} \\\\  & ={{field-2}}\\,\\cdot \\,{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The usual inner product of functions $f$ and $g$ over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ is given by\n\n$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFor a $2\\pi $-periodic function $f(x)$ that is piecewise continuous over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ),$ the Fourier series of $f$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{0},$ ${a}_{n},$ and ${b}_{n}$ are constants to be determined. \n\nNow, we find the inner product of $f(x)$ with $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2},\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩ & = \\\\ \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the functions\n$1,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),…$\nare orthogonal with respect to the defined inner product, the only nonzero term in the final expression above is\n\n$$\n{a}_{6}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(12x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{1}{24}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12x)]}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\pi -(-\\pi ))-\\frac{1}{24}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12\\pi )-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-12\\pi ))) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩ & ={a}_{6}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩ \\\\ {a}_{6} & =\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩} \\\\ {a}_{6} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot {\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }({x}^{3}+5x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-340638/field-1" "q-340638/field-2" "q-340638/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "304c015d-cbb6-5989-a102-d6f0f5f38604"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-340638"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-340648/field-1/54bd993c9957b3f49108f2caafbbb3800ff87f21e4b05ff64a41602eefa31911" :answer/id #uuid "1b77a79b-7ad5-5688-9168-07a38f1b36d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340648/field-1/7325d62f39c3a309dd6bc305b5a72bb949f604039b1487a85b4027a278d92529" :answer/id #uuid "9d5d7661-ca8f-5155-80c1-4f8a6b789161" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340648/field-1/c6b7483690173ffb4df15d4994ac0a2a786b5ddb6b0cbf5dad7468b56aab23a7" :answer/id #uuid "15433997-030c-52b0-ada0-4a3798577c3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩}{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340648/field-1/bd48b2c6f02260fae923e8d9dbc4821377446b76b27c0e5b24e6e17412d1d278" :answer/id #uuid "01c9c309-acdc-5319-a8a0-fca83f00a99a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340648/field-1/6680a24a804e25076d015d923fea1667d00ff2e17e122c764a7d3a028d1d3234" :answer/i